# camera_keys (2026-11-27, D152): the camera keys are Y U I O P (121 117 105 111 112) in the board keybinds.pdl files, so the digits belong to the game.
# Every row the roll-out rewrote carries a marker "(was N; D152)" after its new code, so ONE check per row per file proves it. Only TRACKED files are asserted (a fresh clone has them); the board instance copies git ignores or does not track (draw-battle, dsr-rpg, teario-make, teario-play, the editor) were changed on the owner's machine and on debil, not here.
# NOT in this list on purpose: rta-board and vox-pchq keep the digits (their own game keys use I O and P U). When those game keys move, add their files here.
# The editor and rmmc files were done first, with their own wording (case rmmc_help).
RESULTS | ../results/camera_keys.txt
CASE | every-board-uses-the-letter-camera-keys
SCRATCH
EXPECT_HAS | $HOUSE/@.apps/cdda-hq/keybinds.pdl | 121 # 'y'  first person (was 1; D152) | cdda-hq: y is first person
EXPECT_HAS | $HOUSE/@.apps/cdda-hq/keybinds.pdl | 117 # 'u'  third person (was 2; D152) | cdda-hq: u is third person
EXPECT_HAS | $HOUSE/@.apps/cdda-hq/keybinds.pdl | 105 # 'i'  free roam (was 3; D152) | cdda-hq: i is free roam
EXPECT_HAS | $HOUSE/@.apps/cdda-hq/keybinds.pdl | 111 # 'o'  bird eye (was 4; D152) | cdda-hq: o is bird eye
EXPECT_HAS | $HOUSE/@.apps/cdda-hq/keybinds.pdl | 112 # 'p'  toggle 2D <-> 3D (was 0; D152) | cdda-hq: p toggles 2D and 3D
